To the Abuse Team at {{ provider }},

{% if role == 'registrar' %}
I am writing to report non-consensual intimate imagery (NCII) depicting me that is
being distributed from a domain you sponsor, and to request your urgent intervention.
{% elif role == 'site' %}
I am writing to report non-consensual intimate imagery (NCII) depicting me that is
published on your service, and to request its urgent removal.
{% else %}
I am writing to report non-consensual intimate imagery (NCII) depicting me that is
being distributed on infrastructure you operate, and to request its urgent removal.
{% endif %}

REPORTER
    Name:  {{ name }}
    Email: {{ email }}
{% if postal %}
    Address: {{ postal }}
{% endif %}
    Date:  {{ date }}

I am the individual depicted in the material at the URLs listed below. This material
was published and is being distributed without my consent. I have never authorised
its publication, reproduction or distribution by the operator of this site or by any
other party, and I do not consent to it now.

URLS TO BE REMOVED ({{ urls|length }})

{% for u in urls %}
    {{ u }}
{% endfor %}

LEGAL BASIS

{% if self_recorded %}
Copyright - 17 U.S.C. Section 512(c). I created the material myself and am the sole
owner of the copyright in it. No licence to reproduce, display, perform or distribute
it has ever been granted to anyone. This letter is a formal notification of claimed
infringement under Section 512(c)(3), and the statements required by that subsection
appear at the end of this notice.

{% endif %}
{% if india %}
Information Technology Rules - Rule 3(2)(b) of the Information Technology
(Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021, as amended by
the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code)
Amendment Rules, 2026, notified as G.S.R. 120(E) on 10 February 2026 and in force
from 20 February 2026.

On a complaint by the individual depicted, an intermediary must remove or disable
access to content that exposes a person's private areas, shows them in full or
partial nudity or in a sexual act, or that has been artificially morphed to suggest
the same, WITHIN TWO HOURS of that complaint. The 2026 amendment cut this window
from twenty-four hours to two. This notice is that complaint, and the two-hour
period runs from your receipt of it.

Failure to act within that window costs you the protection from liability that
Section 79 of the Information Technology Act, 2000 would otherwise give you.
Publication of this material is separately an offence under Sections 66E, 67 and
67A of that Act.

I am filing this complaint in parallel with the National Cyber Crime Reporting
Portal at cybercrime.gov.in. Please also provide the name and contact details of
the Grievance Officer you are required to appoint under Rule 3(2), together with
your ticket reference for this complaint.

{% endif %}
TAKE IT DOWN Act - Section 3 of the TAKE IT DOWN Act (Pub. L. No. 119-12). The
notice-and-removal duty under that section has been enforceable since 19 May 2026.
On receipt of a valid request from an identifiable individual depicted in a
non-consensual intimate image, a covered platform must remove the material, and any
known identical copies of it, WITHIN 48 HOURS. The Federal Trade Commission enforces
this provision and has already issued warning letters and opened its complaint portal
for non-compliance. Please treat this notice as starting that 48-hour period.

Knowing publication of non-consensual intimate imagery is also a federal criminal
offence under Section 2 of the same Act.
{% if eu %}

GDPR Article 17 - to the extent you process my personal data within the scope of
Regulation (EU) 2016/679, I additionally exercise my right to erasure. The material
is special-category data under Article 9 concerning my sex life, processed without
any lawful basis and without my consent. Article 12(3) requires a response without
undue delay and in any event within one month.
{% endif %}

Independently of any of the above, this material almost certainly breaches your own
acceptable use policy, which is sufficient grounds for you to act immediately.

WHAT I AM ASKING FOR

{% if role == 'registrar' %}
    1. Require the registrant to remove the material at every URL listed above
       within {{ deadline }}, and suspend the domain if they do not.
{% else %}
    1. Remove or disable access to the material at every URL listed above, and to
       any known identical copies, within {{ deadline }}.
{% endif %}
    2. Confirm to me in writing what you removed and on what date.
    3. Preserve server logs and uploader records relating to this material. I am
       pursuing this further and those records may be required.
    4. Do not disclose my name, email or any part of this notice to the uploader or
       to the site operator beyond what is strictly necessary to effect removal.

If you are not the correct party - for example if you are a reseller, a CDN, or the
upstream of the network actually hosting these files - please forward this notice to
the responsible party and tell me who they are, so I can address them directly.
{% if self_recorded %}

